   - Creates a `buffer_adaptor` with `init_empty` flag, which sets both read and write cursors to 0
   - Uses `adaptor.write()` to write the source data to the buffer
   - The buffer will automatically resize if needed to accommodate the data

The `buffer_adaptor` handles all the low-level operations including memory management, cursor tracking, and buffer resizing automatically.

