   - Creates a new thread-local `block_allocator` instance if one doesn't exist
   - Caches the allocator handle if using `unsafe_entrant` policy
   - Increments the reference count if using `ref_counting` policy

2. **`exit_thread_with_allocator`**: This function calls `allocator.thread_exit()` which:
   - Decrements the reference count if using `ref_counting` policy
   - Resets (destroys) the thread-local allocator when the ref count reaches 0
   - Ensures proper cleanup of thread-local resources

