```cpp
#include <hexi/endian.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <bit>

template<typename T>
void convert_from_big_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    if constexpr (std::endian::native == std::endian::little) {
        value = hexi::byte_swap(value);
    }
    // If native is big endian, no conversion needed
}

template<typename T>
void convert_from_little_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    if constexpr (std::endian::native == std::endian::big) {
        value = hexi::byte_swap(value);
    }
    // If native is little endian, no conversion needed
}

template<std::endian from, std::endian to, typename T>
void convert_endianness_inplace(T& value) {
    // Only convert if source and destination endianness differ
    if constexpr (from != to) {
        value = hexi::byte_swap(value);
    }
    // If from == to, no conversion needed
}
```

**Explanation:**

1. **`convert_from_big_endian_inplace`**: Converts a value from big endian to native endian format in-place.
   - If the native system is little endian, we need to byte swap the value
   - If the native system is big endian, no conversion is needed

2. **`convert_from_little_endian_inplace`**: Converts a value from little endian to native endian format in-place.
   - If the native system is big endian, we need to byte swap the value
   - If the native system is little endian, no conversion is needed

3. **`convert_endianness_inplace`**: Converts a value between two arbitrary endianness formats in-place.
   - If the source (`from`) and destination (`to`) endianness are different, we perform a byte swap
   - If they're the same, no conversion is needed

All functions use `constexpr if` to perform compile-time checks, ensuring zero overhead when no conversion is necessary. The `hexi::byte_swap` function from the Hexi library handles the actual byte swapping operation.

