Looking at the `Hexi` library's `static_buffer` class, I can see it provides template methods `write()` and `read()` for writing and reading primitive types.

For `write_uint32_to_buffer`, I need to use the `write()` method which accepts a reference to the data to write.

For `read_uint32_from_buffer`, I need to use the `read()` method which accepts a pointer to the destination where data will be read.

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/static_buffer.h>
#include <cstdint>

template<size_t buffer_size = 1024>
void write_uint32_to_buffer(hexi::static_buffer<std::byte, buffer_size>& buffer, uint32_t value) {
